# ─── The build's own trust base ────────────────────────────────────────
# The gate jobs install from this lockfile and run from this workflow, so a
# PR touching any of these is a PR editing the machinery that judges it. That
# is not theoretical: the first version of these gates checked out the PR
# head and ran `bun install` from it, so an install script added here would
# have forged both verdicts and could have read the review key. Dependency
# bumps now need an owner's approval — dependabot PRs are few, and this is
# the file that makes "the judge runs only trusted code" true.
# `bunfig.toml` does not exist yet; it is owned pre-emptively because it
# configures the same install.
package.json                        @rhonda-rodododo
bun.lockb                           @rhonda-rodododo
bunfig.toml                         @rhonda-rodododo
lefthook.yml                        @rhonda-rodododo
# vitest's MAIN process executes its config — and the config's globalSetup
# and plugins — and that process writes the result file and owns the exit
# code fleet/verify judges. fleet/verify installs the BASE's config bytes over
# a PR's copy, so an edit here is never in effect on its own PR; what merges,
# though, judges every PR after it. Rooted glob: the root configs only.
/vitest.*.config.ts                 @rhonda-rodododo

